  "_version": "1.0.0",
  "_description": "Discord audit-log → AKSI control ID mapping. Discord is the dominant chat platform for developer/community use cases — distinct demographic from Slack (corporate). AI bots (custom-built, ChatGPT bot extensions, Discord's native Clyde AI) post to public + private servers and act as moderators, message-deleters, and member-routers. The /guilds/{guild.id}/audit-logs endpoint emits action_type integer codes (1..212+) covering guild/channel/role/member/invite/webhook/integration/automod/Clyde-AI events. action_type drives the primary signal; options.count, options.members_removed, max_uses, and the changes[] keys produce additive flags. Discord IDs are pseudonymous snowflakes — capture verbatim. Reasons can carry full PII/IR-narrative; we capture length+sha256 only. Role names can encode org structure; we capture length+sha256 only. changes[] values are NEVER stored — only key names.",
